Cross-recorded from app-game WP21.

Native app coverage in the shared child-facing UX contracts:

- native app and unknown app target kinds can be represented without exposing
  private diagnostics;
- family-rule warning, new-app approval-needed, time almost finished, time
  limit reached, request submitted/approved/denied, manual-required, and
  unavailable states are schema-backed;
- ask-parent/request-more-time states require evidence, child reason, child
  status, and approval request refs;
- manual-required and unavailable states cannot include adapter action refs;
- text-domain copy is checked for calm wording and no private path/process
  fragments.
